The Lead Finder feature shipped reading process.env.SGAI_API_KEY, but the
actual key is set in Vercel as SCRAPEGRAPHAI_API_KEY (confirmed already
present in Production and Preview). Every search was failing with
"Couldn't reach ScrapeGraphAI" because the key was always undefined.

This was supposed to already be fixed before the feature shipped, but the
original (unfixed) version of that commit's patch got applied instead of
the corrected one — this is that same one-line fix, applied directly.
---
 app/actions/leads.ts | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/app/actions/leads.ts b/app/actions/leads.ts
index 9679cd6..3ed7552 100644
--- a/app/actions/leads.ts
+++ b/app/actions/leads.ts
@@ -61,8 +61,9 @@ export interface CommercialLead {
 }
 
 function sgaiKey(): string {
-  const key = process.env.SGAI_API_KEY
-  if (!key) throw new Error("SGAI_API_KEY env var not set — add it in Vercel project settings.")
+  // Matches the name already set in Vercel project settings.
+  const key = process.env.SCRAPEGRAPHAI_API_KEY
+  if (!key) throw new Error("SCRAPEGRAPHAI_API_KEY env var not set — add it in Vercel project settings.")
   return key
 }
 
